Set-Location -LiteralPath $PSScriptRoot
$msg = 'import preview: say how many of these people we can actually reach. Email-only queued 0 was read as no emails were picked up. It counts rows with an email and NO usable phone - a different question - and no tile answered the one being asked, so the only way to check whether a 100-row import had captured its email addresses was to import it and go looking. Adds Usable phone, Usable email and Bad email to the preview, renames Email-only queued to Email only with the plain-language hint has an email but no usable phone, and puts a short hint under every tile so none of them can be misread the same way. Underneath, unknow@unknown was counted as a USABLE address: the domain is in no blocklist, matches no pattern and is nobody typo of a real domain, so two unreachable rows of the first hundred looked emailable - which matters more than it used to because email is now the only channel carrying the booking link. _check_email_quality now rejects a domain with no dot at all and a placeholder vocabulary CRMs actually write when they have no address - unknown, none, na, noemail, tbd and similar. Those rows are flagged on the LEAD with manual_flag bad_email rather than merely described in custom_fields where no send path looks, and the single email send now refuses them exactly as the batch queue already did, because sending to a dead address costs a hard bounce against the domain reputation and makes the real families mail land worse. They still import and are still textable; only the email channel is blocked. The preview warns about them above the confirm button rather than only in a tile. Importer logic otherwise unchanged.'
& "$PSScriptRoot\deploy.ps1" -Message $msg
Write-Output ("DEPLOY_EXIT=" + $LASTEXITCODE)
